    Property APIs: CRUD, search, filters, pagination and nearby search
    
    Phases F and G of the master specification, plus a fix to the README.
    
    Property model, revised
    - Stores what the specification asks for (GeoJSON point + 2dsphere index,
      separate verificationStatus and availabilityStatus) but serialises what
      the React app already consumes (location.lat/lng, `status`, a `verified`
      boolean, a landlord object). toPublicJSON() is the only place that
      translation happens, so 17k lines of working UI need no rewrite.
    - Rent is priced per occupancy, matching the booking form the frontend
      already has. A pre-save hook maintains indexed rentMin/rentMax so rent
      filtering and sorting stay plain indexed queries.
    - Adds gender preference, occupancy tiers, room counts and landmarks,
      which the existing UI displays.
    
    Endpoints
    - GET    /api/properties              search, filter, sort, paginate
    - GET    /api/properties/nearby       radius query, distance per result
    - GET    /api/properties/my-properties
    - GET    /api/properties/:id
    - POST   /api/properties              landlord
    - PUT    /api/properties/:id          landlord, own only
    - DELETE /api/properties/:id          landlord, own only
    
    Rules enforced server-side
    - Ownership comes from the token; a landlord field in the body is ignored.
    - A landlord cannot verify or feature their own listing; editing a
      verified listing returns it to pending.
    - Discoverability: anonymous and tenant callers see only verified, active
      listings; a landlord additionally sees their own; an admin sees all. A
      listing the caller may not see returns 404, not 403, so hidden listings
      cannot be probed by id.
    - Filters requiring several amenities require all of them; a rent range
      matches when any occupancy price falls inside it; a gender search still
      includes listings open to anyone.
    
    Supporting work
    - optionalAuth middleware, so public routes can widen results for a
      landlord or admin without requiring a token.
    - seedProperties script: ten realistic tier-2/tier-3 listings across two
      landlords, including one pending and one occupied fixture so moderation
      and availability are demonstrable.
    - syncIndexes script: Mongoose never drops indexes a schema no longer
      declares, and a stale 2dsphere index makes every insert fail after a
      field changes shape.
    - Test suite grows to 64 (41 new). Each test file now uses its own
      database so files can run in parallel.
    - Removes UTF-16 bytes that a PowerShell "echo >> README.md" appended to
      the README, which had made the file unreadable as text.
    
