    StaySphere backend: foundation, models, auth and role authorization
    
    Phases 1-4 of the backend plan, built with Node.js, Express 5, MongoDB
    and Mongoose.
    
    Phase 1 — Foundation
    - Validated config (fails fast on a missing required variable), single
      MongoDB connection, /health route reporting database state
    - Helmet, CORS restricted to the configured frontend origins, 1 MB body
      cap, rate limiting on the auth endpoints
    - Central error middleware: the only place an error response is shaped,
      so stack traces and driver messages never reach clients
    - app.js / server.js split so the app is importable without opening a
      port or a connection
    
    Phase 2 — Database models
    - User (unique email, passwordHash with select:false, hashing in the
      model so no controller can store plain text)
    - Property (GeoJSON point + 2dsphere index for the nearby search, plus
      compound city/type/rent and text indexes)
    - Booking (BOOKING_TRANSITIONS is the single source of truth for the
      status machine; rent is captured at request time)
    - Payment (server-derived amount, partial unique index allowing one
      successful payment per booking while failed attempts may repeat)
    
    Phase 3 — Authentication
    - POST /api/auth/register, POST /api/auth/login, GET /api/auth/me
    - JWT carrying only id and role; bcrypt password hashing
    - Login returns one message for both unknown email and wrong password,
      so it cannot be used to enumerate accounts
    - Admins cannot be created through public sign-up — seedAdmin.js is the
      only path
    
    Phase 4 — Authorization
    - authorize(...roles) kept separate from protect, so authentication and
      authorization are independently testable
    - Role read from the database record, never from the request body
    
    Also includes seedDemo.js for the demo accounts the frontend advertises,
    and 23 tests on Node's built-in runner (no extra dependencies) covering
    auth, password hashing, token handling, suspended accounts and every
    role combination.
    
    No real payment gateway is integrated; Payment.provider records that the
    flow is a demo.
    
